<!-- 2 Problem -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Context &amp; problem</div>
  <h1>Sensitive documents have to leave the building every day</h1>
  <p class="lead">Medical records, court files, bank statements and lab reports are routinely shared for research, litigation,
    insurance and public-information requests. Every copy must first be stripped of personal data &mdash; today, by hand.</p>
  <div class="grid4" style="margin-bottom:22px">
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Hospitals</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Research &amp; IRB</h3><p>Chart extracts for approved studies must be de-identified before release.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Law firms &amp; courts</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Litigation</h3><p>Filings keep the parties but mask ID numbers, accounts and witnesses.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Government</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Public release</h3><p>Freedom-of-information requests require removing private individuals.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><span class="tag">Insurers &amp; HR</span><h3 style="margin-top:8px">Claims &amp; audits</h3><p>Handwritten forms, ID photos and seals travel to third parties.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid3">
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>Slow &amp; error-prone</h3><p>A reviewer reads every line of every scan, then a second reviewer checks. One missed ID number is a reportable breach.</p></div>
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>Cloud AI is off-limits</h3><p>The documents are exactly the data that policy forbids sending to an external API &mdash; the tool must run on-premises.</p></div>
    <div class="card" style="background:#fff5f2;border-color:#f6c7b8"><h3>Stakes are rising</h3><p>Taiwan's PDPA amendment (promulgated Nov 2025) creates a dedicated regulator and fines up to NT$15 million per failure to rectify.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="src">Sources: K&amp;L Gates, "New Developments in the Taiwan Personal Data Protection Act" (Jan 2026); Baker McKenzie InsightPlus on the 2025 PDPA amendment.</div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span>2</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 3 Why existing tools fail -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Context &amp; problem</div>
  <h1>Why existing approaches fall short</h1>
  <p class="lead">Real documents are scanned, bilingual, handwritten and stamped. Identifiers hide in free text, not just in fixed formats.</p>
  <table class="t">
    <tr><th style="width:30%">Capability</th><th>Manual review</th><th>Regex / DLP tools</th><th>Cloud AI APIs</th><th class="hl" style="background:#1f3a8a">RedactAgent</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Scanned / photographed pages (OCR)</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="part">add-on</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="yes hl">yes &mdash; PP-OCR</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Names, addresses, roles in free text</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="yes hl">yes &mdash; local LLM</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Quasi-identifiers ("the only dentist on Orchid Island")</td><td class="part">if noticed</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="part">partly</td><td class="yes hl">yes + agentic re-check</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Signatures, ID photos, red seals (印章)</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="part">partly</td><td class="yes hl">yes &mdash; local VLM + colour</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Taiwan formats (身分證 checksum, ROC dates, NHI no.)</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="part">custom rules</td><td class="part">weak</td><td class="yes hl">built-in</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Data never leaves the premises</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="yes">yes</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="yes hl">yes</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Purpose-aware (research vs. court vs. public)</td><td class="part">by memory</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="no">no</td><td class="yes hl">policy files</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Throughput &amp; tamper-evident audit trail</td><td class="no">minutes / page</td><td class="yes">fast</td><td class="part">vendor logs</td><td class="yes hl">{{ "%.0f"|format(best.pages_per_min if best else thr.v3.pages_per_minute) }} pages/min + hash chain</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span>3</span></div>
</section>

<!-- 4 Solution overview -->
<section class="slide">
  <div class="kicker">Solution</div>
  <h1>Detect, attack, decide, redact, prove &mdash; all on-prem</h1>
  <p class="lead">Deterministic rules for precision, a local LLM for context, a local VLM for what is not text &mdash;
    and an <b>adversarial agent</b> that tries to re-identify people from the redacted result before anyone releases it.</p>
  <div class="flow" style="margin:6px 0 22px">
    <div class="step"><b>1 &middot; Read</b><span>PDF, scan or phone photo; PP-OCR with per-character boxes, EN + 中文.</span></div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div>
    <div class="step"><b>2 &middot; Detect</b><span><span class="badge b-rule">RULE</span> <span class="badge b-llm">LLM</span> <span class="badge b-vlm">VLM</span> layers run in parallel on two cards.</span></div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div>
    <div class="step" style="border-color:#be185d"><b style="color:#be185d">3 &middot; Attack</b><span>Agent reads the redacted text like an adversary; anything still identifying is added; risk score 0&ndash;100.</span></div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div>
    <div class="step"><b>4 &middot; Decide</b><span>Purpose policy: redact, pseudonymise, keep year only, or keep.</span></div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div>
    <div class="step"><b>5 &middot; Review</b><span>Human approves each box; unread ink flagged.</span></div><div class="arr">&rarr;</div>
    <div class="step"><b>6 &middot; Export &amp; prove</b><span>Pixel-burned PDF, de-identified text, hash-chained audit.</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid3">
    <div class="card"><h3>Finds what regex cannot</h3><p>Names in narratives, the role of each person (patient vs. physician vs. witness),
      quasi-identifiers, handwritten fields, signatures, ID photos and red seals.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Checks its own work</h3><p>Detection asks "what is PII?". The agentic check asks the question that matters for release:
      <i>"could someone still tell who this is?"</i> &mdash; and shows the answer as a risk score.</p></div>
    <div class="card"><h3>Built for production</h3><p>Single document review, batch mode for archives, live system page for operators.
      One command deploys it on a 2&times; B70 host.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="foot"><span>RedactAgent &middot; ASUS UGen AI League 2026 &middot; Final</span><span>4</span></div>
</section>

